# The crossing for a routing column three blocks wide: west-east stays at y = 1
# along the middle row, north-south climbs over it down the middle column, as
# in the crossing tile (whose comments say why the stones keep the two apart).
# The flat arm is three blocks, port, centre, port, so a repeater in it sits
# at the centre under the bridge; the climbing arm has no room for one, and the
# tile cannot be turned to give it one (that takes five blocks across).
tile cross_n
size 3 4 5
port W io 0 1 2
port E io 2 1 2
port N io 1 1 0
port S io 1 1 4
function cross

legend
  G minecraft:glass
  # minecraft:stone
  - minecraft:redstone_wire

layer 0
  .G.
  ...
  GGG
  ...
  .G.
layer 1
  .-.
  .#.
  ---
  .#.
  .-.
layer 2
  ...
  .-.
  .#.
  .-.
  ...
layer 3
  ...
  ...
  .-.
  ...
  ...
